<article class="env-lemma" id="B10CB7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B10CB7">Lemma <span data-tag="B10CB7">5.5.9.15</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a category which admits finite products, and $\mathbf{A}\subseteq \Set _{\Delta }^{\calC }$ be the full subcategory spanned by the product preserving functors. For every object $C \in \calC $, the evaluation map $\mathbf{A}\rightarrow \sSet $ preserves homotopy colimits of simplicial objects. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In view of Corollary <a href="/tag/6D4523" data-tag="6D4523">5.5.9.3</a> and Theorem <a href="/tag/EB2834" data-tag="EB2834">4.2.4.1</a>, it will suffice to show that the evaluation functor $\calP _{\Sigma }( \Nerve (\calC )^{op} ) \rightarrow \sSet $ preserves $\Nerve (\cDelta )^{op}$-indexed colimits. This follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/0C5801" data-tag="0C5801">5.5.8.10</a>, since $\Nerve (\cDelta )^{op}$ is sifted (Lemma <a href="/tag/4D343C" data-tag="4D343C">5.5.8.4</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>